        "description": "Player skin tone (binary): 1 = Dark skin (averaged rater score >= 0.60), 0 = Light skin (averaged rater score <= 0.40). Middle/ambiguous ratings are excluded to sharpen contrast between dark and light. This is the primary independent variable testing whether darker-skinned players get more red cards.",
